At 512 dimensions, MRL truncation has a slight advantage. But as the vectors get smaller, PCA catches up and either beats or matches MRL. 

On `text-embedding-3-small`, PCA is clearly better below 256 dims (65% vs 46% retained at 32). On `qwen3-embedding-8b` the race is much closer (71% vs 68% at 32).

One thing I found interesting is that the MRL training in `qwen3-embedding-8b` is strong enough that its truncated 32-dim vectors, cut from 4,096 dimensions, retain more quality than 3-small's cut from 1,536.

